Subject: [PATCH] plugins: new mtk-ccci plugin (MediaTek SoC modem over CCCI, AT only)

MediaTek SoC modems (MD1) on vendor kernels expose an AT channel on the CCCI
tty (/dev/ttyC0) and the data path on ccmniN network devices, without USB or
PCI ids and without MIPC. The plugin claims those ports by the udev tag
ID_MM_MTK_CCCI and groups them by ID_MM_PHYSDEV_UID (77-mm-mtk-ccci.rules).

- powers the MD up (+CFUN=1) before the SIM checks, sends AT+EDALLOW=1
- swallows the proprietary URCs that otherwise break response parsing
- data: +CGDCONT + +CGACT=1,<cid>; the "+EIF: <id>, ifup, <cid>, <ipv4>"
  report selects ccmni<id % 100>; static IPv4 /32 without gateway, DNS from
  +CGCONTRDP, address fallback from +CGPADDR; unexpected "ifdown" reports the
  bearer disconnected, "ifchg" keeps it
- voice: +ECPI call progress mapped to call states, +CLCC for the rest, ATH
  for hangup all
- unit tests for the +EIF, +ECPI, +CGCONTRDP, +CGPADDR parsers and +COPS AcT

Adapted in part from the mtk-soc plugin of the MT6895-Mainline
modemmanager-mtk-soc fork (GPL-2.0-or-later).
---
